---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/Briefing.css';
---

<Layout title="ORION // OP 5: Hollow March - Briefing" description="Field briefing for Operation Hollow March - a three-target deception raid staged to read as a Finnish breakthrough, Zone-21 Finland." nav={[{ href: '/orion-fimbulwinter/mission-control/', label: '<- MISSION CONTROL' }, { href: '#situation', label: 'SITUATION' }, { href: '#mission', label: 'MISSION' }, { href: '#ground', label: 'GROUND' }, { href: '#execution', label: 'EXECUTION' }, { href: '#roe', label: 'ROE' }, { href: '#support', label: 'SUPPORT' }]} footer="ORION INTERNATIONAL - ZONE-21 // FIMBULWINTER - OP 5: HOLLOW MARCH - BRIEFING" decryptLines={['ORION SECURE UPLINK - CHANNEL 21', 'AUTHENTICATING OPERATOR...', 'CLEARANCE CONFIRMED - FIELD COMMAND', 'DECRYPTING DOSSIER: OPERATION HOLLOW MARCH']}>
  <div class="briefing-actions"><button class="print-opord" type="button">PRINT OPORD</button></div>
  <section id="situation" class="briefing-section"><h1 class="op-name">SITUATION</h1><h2 class="op-title">OPERATION HOLLOW MARCH</h2><div class="reveal"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A week of scattered contact along the rest of the line has done more damage to morale than to ground. FDF brigades further north and east are being pushed back mile by mile — corporate assessments circulating this week rate the broader Finnish counter-effort as barely holding, let alone advancing. Command sees the opening: if Chernov already expects Finland to be losing everywhere, a sudden, convincing breakthrough somewhere quiet will read as real.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion's actual target is local: a handful of outposts feeding the 44th's rear. But the effect has to look national. If the 44th believes a Finnish spearhead has punched through behind their line, they pull forces off the front to deal with it — and the real front, the one FDF is actually losing, gets room to breathe.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Three objectives make the lie, all in one night. A bridge carrying Russian reinforcement traffic toward the front. A distribution point feeding that traffic. A communications relay Orion will use to put one message on the corps net, in Finnish military form, claiming the position — and by extension the ground around it — for Finland.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">This is behind enemy lines, in depth. Expect patrols between objectives, roadblocks on the connecting roads, and standing garrisons at each site — none of this ground is undefended rear area, it's occupied territory with a schedule.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion's fingerprints stay off all three objectives. If this reads as Orion, it's a raid. If it reads as Finland, it's an invasion.</p></div></section>
  <section id="mission" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">MISSION</h2><h3 class="op-title">TASKING</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">FIELD COMMAND DIRECTIVE</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion elements will destroy the bridge carrying Russian reinforcements toward the frontline; sabotage the distribution point supplying that route; seize the communications relay and transmit a claim, in Finnish military form, that the position has been taken by Finnish forces; then exfil via Valkyrie. All three objectives and exfil are to be completed within a single night.</p></div></section>
  <section id="ground"><h2 class="op-name">GROUND</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD NAVIGATION</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">TERRAIN // SECTOR UNSPECIFIED</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A river crossing carrying the 44th's reinforcement route toward the front (Phase 1), garrisoned. A forward distribution point supplying that route (Phase 2), garrisoned. A communications relay covering the wider sector, tied into the corps net (Phase 3), garrisoned. An exfil point within Valkyrie's reach of the relay (Phase 4). Roads connecting the objectives carry Russian patrols and roadblocks — this is not empty ground between targets.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12px;">Exact positions and the exfil point are released to ground command once Eden placement is locked. Positions are directional, not gridded.</p></div></section>
  <section id="execution" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">EXECUTION</h2><h3 class="op-title">ORDER OF BATTLE</h3><div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-1" data-phase="1"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="1" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 1 / 4</div><h3>Cut the Bridge</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Reach and destroy the crossing, garrison in place. The objective is the structure, not the ground either side of it — do not hold, do not engage traffic that isn't defending the objective or blocking the approach. A dropped bridge reads as denial. A firefight sprawled across both banks reads as an ambush. Command needs the first.</p></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-2" data-phase="2"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="2" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 2 / 4</div><h3>Break the Line</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Move to the distribution point, expect a standing garrison and possible reinforcement from the roadblocks en route. Destroy stock and infrastructure on site; this is denial, not a raid for matériel — nothing here needs to leave with the team.</p></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-3" data-phase="3"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="3" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 3 / 4</div><h3>The Hollow Claim</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Breach and clear the communications relay. Hold it long enough to get one transmission out: a claim, in Finnish military form and terminology, that the position has been taken and is being held by Finnish forces. No Orion identifiers on the traffic, on the position, or on anything left behind. If it can be read as Finnish, leave it. If it can be read as Orion, remove it or burn it.</p></div><div class="phase climax reveal" id="execution-phase-4" data-phase="4"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="4" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 4 / 4</div><h3>Exfil</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Break from the relay to the designated pickup point. Valkyrie is assigned for extraction this operation — plan the timing of Phase 3 around the extraction window, not the other way around. Expect the route out to draw the same patrols and roadblocks the route in did, now alerted.</p></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim); font-size:12px;">Ground commanders retain discretionary authority over internal task allocation and approach across all phases.</p></div></section>
  <section id="roe" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">RULES OF ENGAGEMENT</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD RESTRICTIONS</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">ROE // EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY</div><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li>Any Russian element, garrison, patrol, or roadblock observed, in contact, or confirmed at a designated objective is hostile.</li><li>This operation's value is in what the 44th believes happened, not in what Orion destroys. Phases 1 and 2 are denial objectives — do not hold ground, do not seek contact beyond what's needed to complete the task or clear the approach.</li><li>Nothing recovered or left at any objective may identify Orion. Where a choice exists between an outcome that reads as Finnish and one that reads as Orion, take the Finnish one.</li><li>The transmission in Phase 3 is the operation's centerpiece and is not to be improvised past its stated form — Finnish military phrasing and format, nothing that invites verification.</li><li>Lethal force is authorised against confirmed hostile positions without further clearance.</li><li>Self-defence is authorised at all times without prior command approval.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section id="support" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">SUPPORT</h2><h3 class="op-title">AVAILABLE ASSETS</h3><div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">AIR SUPPORT</div><h3>Valkyrie</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Assigned for exfil and CAS this operation. Coordinate pickup timing against Phase 3 completion; do not extend the hold on the relay waiting for an airframe that isn't inbound yet.</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">COMMS</div><h3>No Liaison</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">No dedicated liaison. Sector traffic is unconfirmed until corroborated.</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">GROUND</div><h3>No Lift</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">No dedicated lift for Phases 1-3. Movement between objectives is on foot, through terrain that isn't yours, on a clock that doesn't wait.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="operator-note" class="operator-note reveal" aria-label="Operator's note"><div class="head">OFF-RECORD // FOR THE PERSON WHO READS TO THE END</div><p>You're not going to win this war tonight. You're going to make Chernov think someone else is, somewhere else, and pull men off a line that's already breaking anyway.</p><p>Nobody back home will ever hear Hollow March was Orion. That's the job working. If it's ever told at all, it'll be told as a Finnish miracle — and you'll be the only ones who know it wasn't.</p><p>Leave nothing behind that says otherwise. Not a scrap, not a casing with the wrong stamp, not a body in the wrong uniform. The lie only holds if it's clean.</p></section>
  <script>
    const unlockPhase = (phase: string) => {
      const blip = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`.blip[data-phase="${phase}"]`);
      if (!blip) return;
      blip.classList.remove('locked');
      blip.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
      blip.removeAttribute('tabindex');
    };
    document.querySelectorAll('.blip').forEach((blip) => blip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const target = document.querySelector(blip.dataset.target || '');
      if (!(target instanceof HTMLElement) || blip.classList.contains('locked')) return;
      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reducedMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      target.classList.remove('flash');
      void target.offsetWidth;
      target.classList.add('flash');
      window.setTimeout(() => target.classList.remove('flash'), 1500);
    }));
    const phaseObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting || !(entry.target instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
        const phase = entry.target.dataset.phase;
        if (!phase) return;
        unlockPhase(phase);
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.45 });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.phase[data-phase]').forEach((phase) => phaseObserver.observe(phase));

    const checklistKey = 'orion-checklist-op5';
    const completePhases = new Set<number>(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(checklistKey) || '[]'));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-checklist-phase]').forEach((input) => {
      const phase = Number(input.dataset.checklistPhase);
      input.checked = completePhases.has(phase);
      input.addEventListener('change', () => {
        input.checked ? completePhases.add(phase) : completePhases.delete(phase);
        localStorage.setItem(checklistKey, JSON.stringify([...completePhases]));
      });
    });

    document.querySelector('.print-opord')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  </script>
</Layout>
